Mycena inclinata , commonly known as the clustered bonnet or the oak @-@ stump bonnet cap , is a species of mushroom in the family Mycenaceae . The doubtfully edible mushroom has deep tan cap and vaguely raised dark brown stem . Its flesh is thin and white when young and becomes substantially thick and gelatinous when older .
